    verse: "Do not despise these small beginnings, for the Lord rejoices to see the work begin.",
    reflection: "You're frustrated because progress feels slow. But small wins matter. Every step forward, no matter how small, is progress. You woke up and prayed - that's a win. You chose kindness when you wanted to snap - that's growth. You paid an extra $50 on debt - that's momentum. Don't despise small beginnings or incremental progress. God celebrates the work beginning, not just the work completed. Every giant was once a baby. Every oak was once an acorn. Every marathon begins with one step. Small, consistent actions over time produce massive results. The key is consistency. Keep showing up. Keep trying. Keep believing. Today, celebrate one small win. Acknowledge your progress, however minor it seems. Thank God for how far you've come. Small wins compound into big victories.",
