    reflection: "Life doesn't happen by accident; it happens by intention. Intentional people don't drift; they direct. They set goals, make plans, and execute with purpose. Without intentionality, you'll waste time, miss opportunities, and live reactively instead of proactively. Intentionality applies to everything: relationships (schedule time), health (plan meals), finances (create budgets), faith (establish rhythms). Wise living isn't complicated; it's intentional. Today, evaluate your life. Are you living by design or default? What needs more intention - your marriage, parenting, career, faith, friendships? Pick one area and set a specific goal this week. Write it down. Tell someone. Take action. Don't let life happen to you. Happen to life. Be intentional.",
