    scripture: "1 Corinthians 10:13",
    verse: "No temptation has overtaken you except what is common to mankind. And God is faithful; he will not let you be tempted beyond what you can bear. But when you are tempted, he will also provide a way out so that you can endure it.",
    reflection: "Addiction feels like chains you can't break. But freedom is possible. Not through willpower alone, but through God's power combined with practical steps. Admit you have a problem. Bring it into the light. Tell someone you trust. Get professional help - counseling, rehab, support groups. Identify triggers and avoid them. Replace the addiction with healthy habits. Build accountability. This isn't about perfection; it's about progress. You might relapse, but that doesn't mean you failed - it means you're human. Get back up. Keep fighting. God doesn't condemn you; He empowers you. His grace is sufficient. His power is made perfect in weakness. Freedom is yours in Christ. Today, take one step: call a counselor, attend a meeting, confess to a friend, delete the app. Break one chain. Freedom is worth fighting for.",
