    verse: "Each of you should use whatever gift you have received to serve others, as faithful stewards of God's grace in its various forms.",
    reflection: "God gave you unique gifts, talents, and passions - not for your glory, but for His purposes and others' good. Your gifts aren't random; they're intentional. They reveal how God wants to use you to impact the world. Maybe you're a natural encourager, gifted teacher, creative artist, strategic thinker, or compassionate servant. Don't compare your gifts to others. Don't covet their calling. Use what God gave you. Steward your gifts by developing them, deploying them, and using them to serve. Your gifts are needed. There's someone only you can reach, a problem only you can solve, a message only you can deliver. Don't bury your talents. Today, identify one gift God gave you. How can you use it this week to serve someone? Deploy your gift. Steward your calling.",
