    verse: "Now it is required that those who have been given a trust must prove faithful.",
    reflection: "Everything you have is a trust from God: your time, talent, treasure, influence, relationships. None of it is truly 'yours' - it's His, entrusted to you. Stewardship asks: what are you doing with what God gave you? Faithful stewards manage wisely, invest strategically, and give generously. They don't hoard or waste. Are you stewarding your finances well - budgeting, saving, giving? Your time - investing in what matters? Your influence - pointing people to Jesus? Your body - treating it as God's temple? One day you'll give an account. Not to earn salvation - that's grace. But to show faithfulness with what He entrusted. Today, evaluate one area: finances, time, health, relationships. How are you stewarding it? What needs to change? Faithful stewardship honors God and positions you for more.",
