    title: "Breaking Free from Comparison",
    scripture: "2 Corinthians 10:12",
    verse: "We do not dare to classify or compare ourselves with some who commend themselves. When they measure themselves by themselves and compare themselves with themselves, they are not wise.",
    reflection: "Comparison is a joy thief. When you measure your chapter 3 against someone else's chapter 20, you'll always feel behind. Social media makes this worse - everyone's posting highlights while you're living real life. But comparison is foolish. You don't know their whole story, their struggles, or what it cost them. And even if you did, their journey isn't yours. God gave you a unique race to run. Stop looking sideways and start looking up. Focus on your growth, not someone else's. Celebrate their win without diminishing yours. Run your race with endurance. The only comparison that matters is this: are you more like Jesus today than yesterday? Today, notice when comparison creeps in. Stop it. Thank God for your unique journey. Celebrate someone else's win genuinely.",
