    reflection: "Your real enemy isn't people - it's spiritual forces. When relationships break, temptation intensifies, or circumstances crumble, recognize there's a spiritual battle. The enemy wants to kill, steal, and destroy. But you're not defenseless. God gave you armor: truth, righteousness, peace, faith, salvation, the Word, and prayer. Fight with these weapons. When lies attack, speak truth. When temptation comes, quote Scripture. When fear rises, worship. When opposition increases, pray. Don't fight people; fight spiritual forces through spiritual weapons. Stand firm. Don't retreat. The battle is real, but so is your authority in Christ. The victory is already won; you're enforcing it. Today, identify one spiritual attack you're facing. Speak Scripture over it. Pray against it. Stand firm.",
